.TH PERVIUS-KILLSWITCH 1 "2026-11-18" "Pervius" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pervius\-killswitch \- control the Pervius VPN kill switch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pervius\-killswitch
.B status
.br
.B pervius\-killswitch
.BR arm " [" \-\-allow\-lan "] [" \-\-allow\-interface
.IR IFACE " ...]"
.br
.B pervius\-killswitch
.BR configure " [" \-\-allow\-lan "] [" \-\-allow\-interface
.IR IFACE " ...]"
.br
.B pervius\-killswitch
.BR update\-endpoints " [" \-\-merge ]
.br
.B pervius\-killswitch
.BR disarm " | " diagnose
.SH DESCRIPTION
Talks to the
.B pervius\-killswitchd
system service over D-Bus. Every change is authorized by polkit.
While armed, the service installs the nftables table
.B inet pervius_ks
that allows only loopback, the Pervius tunnel interface
.B pervius0
and any interfaces you always allow, DHCP, IPv6 neighbour discovery and the
VPN server addresses of the Pervius-managed profile, and drops all other
traffic.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the service state.
.TP
.BR arm " [" \-\-allow\-lan "] [" \-\-allow\-interface " IFACE]"
Install the rules for the managed profile.
.B \-\-allow\-lan
also allows RFC 1918 and ULA local-network ranges;
.B \-\-allow\-interface
(repeatable) always allows an interface such as
.BR wt0 .
.TP
.BR configure " [" \-\-allow\-lan "] [" \-\-allow\-interface " IFACE]"
Change LAN access and the allowed interfaces while armed, in one atomic
update.
.TP
.BR update\-endpoints " [" \-\-merge ]
Resolve the managed profile's VPN server names again and replace the allowed
server addresses in one atomic update
.RB ( \-\-merge
keeps the current addresses as well). While the tunnel is down, the service
resolves through a DNS window of at most five seconds that admits only its
own queries.
.TP
.B disarm
Remove the rules. Use this to recover network access if the kill switch was
left armed.
.TP
.B diagnose
Read-only checks of nftables, the service and platform details.
.SH RECOVERY
If the service itself is broken, remove the table as root:
.B nft delete table inet pervius_ks
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pervius (1),
.BR nft (8)
